        "created_at": "2015-03-08T15:29:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We realized it would probably be easier to know what’s going on if everyone could see the nominations as they are happening.&nbsp; <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\">  (Plus it will eliminate the “Oh, someone probably nominated them” issue.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"> ) We’ve created two threads for folks to post nominations in: this thread for nominating forumites and <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/public-postthread-nomination-thread-forum-awards-2014-7009\">a second thread for nominating posts/threads</a>.<br><br>The awards for forumites are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Inspiring Presence (Morale Booster) – The forum member who, through positive attitude and kind heart, did the most to make the Greater Than Games forums a positive experience over the past year</li>\n<li>Bolster Allies (Funniest) – The forum member who was best at making people laugh and providing humorous moments over the past year</li>\n<li>Truth Seeker (Lore Master) – The forum member who has done the best job answering questions (rules, facts, mythology, etc.) and otherwise providing useful and accurate information over the past year</li>\n<li>Harmony (Top Debater) – The forum member who is best at rationally debating positions (without turning it into a fight) over the past year</li>\n<li>Exceeded Expectations (Top Contributor) – The forum member who contributed to the Greater Than Games community with tools and/or accessories the most (including wiki contributions) over the past year</li>\n<li>Unique Capabilities (Top Artist) – The forum member who created the best/most Greater Than Games-related art or fanfic over the past year</li>\n</ul>\n<br>If you want to nominate someone, you can either post here with their name and the award you're nominating them for or use <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1xheeWop4_jfcOelIcNUKLBBtDLw-lCgjXtKPub5DQIk/viewform?usp=send_form\">the original form for anonymous nominations</a>. For posts here, you can also include a link to an example of their contributions and/or a quick blurb explaining why you're nominating someone. Such a blurb shouldn't be more than a sentence (to avoid it turning into campaigning). If you want to nominate someone who's already been nominated, feel free.\n<p>And feel free to include multiple nominations in each post.</p>\n<p>Someone nominated for an award for different specific reasons will still only be listed once in the voting - we won't be splitting votes due to multiple contributions.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/gtg-forum-award-nominations-2014-5454\">Rules are posted in the original nominations thread</a>.</p>\n<p>We'll be posting the nominations that have already been made anonymously, and we'll continue to post those that come in for the next couple of weeks.</p>",
